-# Bootstrap procedure and failures, 2026-11-10
-
-Purpose: improve future initialization of an Ultrastable project (idea to private repos to local copy).
-
-## What worked
-1. Draft each repo as files in the project Library (ultrastable-repos/), one folder per planned repo, with an index README.
-2. Commit each repo as a git bundle (ultrastable-git/) plus push-all.sh, so a push is one command once repos exist.
-3. Copy to the local folder with device_commit_files, one file per entry, 40-45 per call, then verify with a recursive device_list_dir.
-4. Keep every deliverable as a file, never only in a thread.
-
-## Failures and fixes
-- Cloud sessions cannot create GitHub repos. Rowan (or an owner) must create the org repos and install the Claude GitHub App before any push. Ask for this at the start, not at the end.
-- add_repo on ultrastable/site returned "not found or no access" at 08:22; repos appeared later (all private by 09:30). Re-check list_repos instead of assuming.
-- Computer sessions on QNFO-WIN failed to start three times. Prefer folder access; do not depend on a device shell.
-- Remote device tools refuse to write .github and .claude paths (7 files). Workaround: the git bundles carry them; push from a machine with a shell. Next time plan the bundle path first.
-- Another thread was writing a duplicate ultrastable/ folder and a zip at the same time. Assign one owner per Library path before starting.
-- The Library is a network mount: file counts changed mid-run. Take the file list once, then copy from that list.
-
-## Improvements for next init
-- Step 0: confirm org, repos, GitHub App and device folder access exist; list what is missing in one message.
-- Make the seed's bootstrap.py check these preconditions and print a plain pass/fail table.
-- Never make a site public or deploy it before the provisional patent is filed. Deploy means: private repos pushed, nothing on a public domain.
