-# Bootstrapping lessons: the business-plan thread (2026-11-10)
-
-What happened when a thread had to produce the business plan and get it onto GitHub, and what the seed should do differently.
-
-## Procedure that worked
-1. Read the roadmap, IP checklist and concept docs first, so the plan matched what already existed.
-2. Research competitors and events with dated sources before writing; mark estimates "est." and unsourced numbers "planning guess".
-3. Write one markdown file per manager persona, with an index README carrying the disclosure tags (SAFE NOW / AFTER FILING / NDA ONLY) and [LAWYER] / [ACCOUNTANT] flags.
-4. Link it from the roadmap (BIZ-2) and the repo README; commit to a git bundle so the history is ready to push.
-5. Once the repo was attached, compare the Library files byte for byte against GitHub before pushing. They were identical (another thread had already pushed), so no duplicate push.
-6. Run an independent review pass on claims. It caught one unsourced market-size number.
-
-## Failures and fixes
-| Failure | Cause | Fix for future initialization |
-|---|---|---|
-| Output first went to a Claude Doc and the Library only | Started before Rowan's rule "if it's not in code, it doesn't exist" was in the project instructions | Seed the rule in project instructions on day 0; the first artifact is always a file in a repo |
-| `add_repo` said "not found" for ultrastable repos | Repos did not exist yet; cloud sessions cannot create repos | Bootstrap checklist step 0: owner creates the empty private repos and installs the Claude GitHub App; the session checks `add_repo` before drafting content that depends on it |
-| `add_repo` first call failed with an empty owner | Passed `owner/repo` as one string | Pass `owner` and `repo` separately |
-| Device shell would not start | Rowan's computer had too little free disk space (the workspace needs up to 17 GB) | Preflight: check free disk before relying on the device; do not make the device the only route |
-| Remote Control session failed to start | Claude Code could not start in the chosen folder on the device | Treat Remote Control as best effort; have a second route (owner runs a one-line `gh repo create` loop, or a cloud-side token with repo-create scope) |
-| Git in the scratch directory refused to run ("dubious ownership") and `rsync` was missing | Fresh container | Use `git -c safe.directory='*'` and `cp -a` in bootstrap scripts |
-| Waited for the owner on a blocked step | Asked instead of probing every route | Rule from Rowan: try every route, then proceed; do not wait on an answer |
-| A market-size number went into the pitch unsourced | Written from memory | Every number in a pitch file needs a source link or a "planning guess" label before commit |
-
-## Deploy status
-Nothing in the business plan is deployed, by design. The site stays unpublished until the provisional is filed (roadmap WEB-2, gate FILED). The plan is documentation in the private `business` repo.
